==Enemy==
Le'boin has high health, attack power and range (400, the same range as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]]), allowing him to easily destroy many units within his expansive reach. However, the major downsides to this tank are his slowish attack rate and movement speed. Even with his weaknesses, this enemy is a major threat early on, as his range is long enough to hit every [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cat]] and purchasable [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]].

Le'boin and most of his variants also have very short backswing, often allowing them to move forward a little after every attack (assuming nothing survives).

In stages like [[Liar's Fate]] and [[Celestial Seas]], he acts as a weaker but faster-attacking [[THE SLOTH]] as he has only one knockback and attacks quicker, making him more of a support-type enemy.

==Strategy==
Le'boin is a dangerous enemy early on in the game. When you first meet him in [[Denmark (Empire of Cats)|Denmark/Shizuoka]], prepare for a long and painful battle because [[Those Guys]] are constantly being spawned. To kill him, you will need to let him and the peons come within range of the [[Cat Cannon]], then fire it and whale on Le'boin with [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cats]], [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cats]] and meatshields.

Later in the game, Le'boin becomes much less dangerous due to the player having [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] and potentially many units that outrange him or are able to hit him with indirect fire, becoming more of a giant money bag than a huge threat, as his health also pales when compared to enemies accompanying him. However, keep him away from your main attackers as he still does enough damage to one-shot many units in [[Stories of Legend]] and [[Legend Stages#Uncanny Legends Stages|Uncanny Legends]].

