==Trivia==
*The Japanese word ''boin'' (ぼいん or ボイン) can mean "with a wham", referring to how he slams his trunk down to attack, or "big breasts", referring to his taste in women.
*Most of his variants' Japanese descriptions are rather risqué, with some even making it to English. Notably, Le'boin's [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|original English description]] is even more explicit.
**[[Le'noir]] collects rare sexy videos and isn't afraid to attack anyone getting too close, knowing the consequences if others learn his secret.
**[[Le'Solar]] has a dark history of appearing in sexy videos.
**[[Le'Behemoth]] sold his soul for pleasurable photos, going as far as defending himself with a Shield. The photos are described as ムフフな ''mafufu na''; マフフ ''mafufu'' is an onomatopoeia for mischievous or conspicuous laughter, similar to "tee hee", but the adjectival form ムフフな ''mafufu na'' generally has the connotations of something being so sexy so you can't help but laugh.
**[[Elephantidae Papaou]] is a "[https://japantoday.com/category/features/lifestyle/from-carnivores-to-herbivores-how-men-are-defined-in-japan carnivorous man]" who got his scars from harassing and being rejected by the ladies, to the point where he developed countless immunities to various effects.
**[[Le'Prude]] is a public morals committee member who confiscates lewd things, but turns red when seeing them and secretly collects them out of curiosity.

